  "title": "The knot's junction is a similitude, and unbranched twists count in polynomial time",
  "subject": "Counting colourings of the knot's incidence graphs under sign classes other than the knot's own",
  "conclusion": "At a trisum square, a side carrying the knot's own signs acts on the other closed side as a similitude of the matchgate identity with multiplier alpha^2 + alpha beta + beta^2, the norm of its split at the knot's angle pi/3. So counting stays polynomial under every sign class unless some square has twisted sides on all three branches.",
